  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), the most fundamental uncertainty is whether image features carry any discriminative signal at all. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest test of this question: it changes only the modality (RNA → image) while holding profile setting (singleprofile) constant, enabling a direct 1-variable comparison against the baseline. If image-only performs comparably or better, it justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion; if it performs substantially worse, we can deprioritize image-dependent configurations and focus budget on RNA encoder and profile/aggregation variants. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because the modality decision gates an entire branch of the search space."
}

